course: dictionary
lesson: 14103
title: Mercifully: luckily or kindly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mercifully means luckily, in a way you feel thankful for, because something bad was avoided or ended. «Mercifully, nobody was hurt when the bus skidded.» The word tells you the writer is glad, because the bad thing did not happen.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Luckily, nobody was hurt when the bus skidded» still makes sense, so luckily is right. Mercifully often shows relief, like saying "thank goodness".
explain: The older meaning is about mercy, which means being kind and forgiving, the way a judge or king might be. «The king acted mercifully and let the prisoner go free.» The clue is that the king forgave someone, not that anyone was lucky.
fact: Mercifully means luckily, or in a way you are thankful for.
fact: «Mercifully» often means "thank goodness": «The test was mercifully short.»
fact: «Mercifully» can also mean in a kind and forgiving way, showing mercy.
fact: Phrases to remember: «mercifully short» and «mercifully, it stopped raining».
fact: Context clues tell you which meaning fits: relief for luck, or forgiveness for mercy.
exercise: «Mercifully, nobody was hurt when the car skidded.» What does mercifully mean here? | Angrily, with a shout | *Luckily, and we are thankful | Loudly, for everyone to hear | Slowly and carefully
exercise: «The king acted mercifully and let the prisoner go free.» What does mercifully mean here? | *In a kind and forgiving way | Quickly, before lunch | Sadly, with tears | Rudely, without any care
exercise: «The film was mercifully short, so we were home by eight.» Which words show relief? | *Mercifully short, meaning thank goodness it was short | Short and rude | Very long and boring | Quietly and slowly
test: Pick the best meaning: «Mercifully, it stopped raining just as we reached the tent.» | Slowly, one drop at a time | Quietly, in a whisper | *Luckily, the rain stopped and we were thankful | Sadly, the rain got worse
test: The judge looked at the young thief and acted mercifully. What does this mean? | Angrily, with a loud voice | *With mercy, by forgiving him kindly | Without any care at all | Harshly, with no chance given
exam: Which sentence uses mercifully to mean luckily? | *«Mercifully, the storm missed our village.» | «She ran mercifully fast.» | «He walked mercifully slowly.»
